    "Both trials show one current AudioFlinger input, one policy input/client and one active target configuration, with voice-recognition mono16kHz PCM16/built-in input and no observed mute/silencing cause.",
    "Trial1 frame counters advance while the logged50ms power history remains at eight low-level bins, maximum -76.3dB; its actual captured PCM metrics report NO_AUDIO_SIGNAL.",
    "Trial2 frame counters advance and reported power rises to -14.0dB; speech reaches the app but the exact expected transcript guard fails.",
    "The observable Android route differs only in newly allocated I/O/port identities. These snapshots do not establish a competing current Android input or an SDK-internal selected-input mismatch.",
    "The first loss is visible in reported HAL power before the decoder. The second requires waveform fidelity and exact replay analysis rather than a missing-input explanation."
